  "skill_summaries": {
    "ultimate": "AoE sleep nearby enemies and heal allies",
    "skill1": "leap forward at battle start, interrupting nearby enemies and creating a healing zone",
    "skill2": "stun an enemy while gaining a shield",
    "skill3": "battle damage taken reduction",
    "skill4": "enhance healing zone healing; reduce skill cooldown whenever ally is healed by zone",
    "skill5": "battle-start leap stuns enemies instead of interrupting"
  },
  "play_overview": "[[Gerda]] opens with a battle-start leap that interrupts nearby enemies and drops a healing zone where she lands. Her ultimate sleeps foes in range while healing allies, turning clustered lines into a stall window. A stun skill adds a personal shield, and damage reduction keeps her standing through the opener. Enhanced zone healing and cooldown reduction on zone heals keep her rotation moving while allies stay inside. She is strongest when enemies bunch up in her zone, while spread formations and sleep- or interrupt-immune foes waste much of her control.",
  "counter_overview": "[[Gerda]] leaps at battle start, remains Unaffected during the cast, and drops a healing spring before her ultimate sleeps clustered foes. Do not bank on interrupting the leap; spread so the stomp and spring cover fewer tiles, then use [[Lily May]] to catch the later sleep wind-up. Pressure her with early high-damage melee like [[Himmel]] or [[Shakir]], and lock the spring with [[filter:heal-inhibitor]] like [[Dunlingr]] alongside that burst. She relocates into the line, so lasting coverage like [[Shemira]] is safer than a single assassin pin."
}
